---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';

const title = 'CKD Stages by GFR: KDIGO G1–G5 and Albuminuria Categories';
const description =
	'Chronic kidney disease stages explained: the KDIGO GFR categories G1 to G5, albuminuria categories A1 to A3, what each eGFR range means, and how CKD is diagnosed.';
---

<Layout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	modified="2026-10-23"
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'CKD Stages', href: '/ckd-stages' }]}
	schema={[
		{
			'@type': 'Article',
			headline: title,
			description,
			mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/ckd-stages#webpage' },
			dateModified: '2026-10-23',
			datePublished: '2026-10-23',
			author: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/#organization' },
			publisher: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/#organization' },
			image: 'https://gfrcalc.com/og-image.png',
		},
	]}
>
	<article class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
			<Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'CKD Stages' }]} />
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
				CKD stages by GFR: the KDIGO classification
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Chronic kidney disease (CKD) is classified using two measurements: the estimated
				glomerular filtration rate (eGFR), which describes how well the kidneys filter blood, and
				albuminuria, which describes how much albumin leaks into the urine. The KDIGO guideline
				combines them into a "cause, GFR category, albuminuria category" system. This guide
				explains each category. To get your own number, use the
				<a href="/" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">GFR calculator</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-faint">Last updated October 23, 2026</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">GFR categories (G1 to G5)</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				GFR categories are defined by eGFR in mL/min/1.73m&sup2;. Higher numbers mean better
				filtration.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline">
				<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
					<caption class="sr-only">KDIGO GFR categories</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-hairline-soft">
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Category</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">eGFR (mL/min/1.73m&sup2;)</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Terms</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G1</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&ge; 90</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Normal or high</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G2</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">60&ndash;89</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Mildly decreased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G3a</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">45&ndash;59</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Mildly to moderately decreased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G3b</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">30&ndash;44</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Moderately to severely decreased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G4</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">15&ndash;29</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Severely decreased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">G5</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&lt; 15</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Kidney failure</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Note that G1 and G2 do not by themselves mean CKD. They count as CKD only when another
				marker of kidney damage is present, such as albuminuria, urine sediment abnormalities,
				structural abnormalities on imaging, or a kidney transplant.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Albuminuria categories (A1 to A3)</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Albuminuria is usually measured as the urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio (ACR) on a
				spot urine sample. At the same eGFR, more albumin in the urine means higher risk of
				progression and of cardiovascular disease.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline">
				<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
					<caption class="sr-only">KDIGO albuminuria categories</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-hairline-soft">
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Category</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">ACR (mg/g)</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">ACR (mg/mmol)</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Terms</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">A1</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&lt; 30</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&lt; 3</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Normal to mildly increased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">A2</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">30&ndash;300</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">3&ndash;30</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Moderately increased</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">A3</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&gt; 300</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">&gt; 30</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">Severely increased</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">How CKD is diagnosed</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				KDIGO defines CKD as abnormalities of kidney structure or function that are present for
				more than three months and that affect health. In practice that means an eGFR below 60
				mL/min/1.73m&sup2; or a marker of kidney damage (most commonly albuminuria), confirmed on
				repeat testing. One low result can be caused by dehydration, a recent illness, intense
				exercise, a high-meat meal, or certain medicines, which is why clinicians repeat the test
				before drawing conclusions.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">What the stages mean in practice</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				<li><strong>G1&ndash;G2:</strong> Kidney function is normal or mildly reduced. Care focuses on managing risk factors such as blood pressure, blood sugar, and albuminuria when it is present.</li>
				<li><strong>G3a&ndash;G3b:</strong> Function is moderately reduced. Clinicians typically review medicines for kidney safety and check for complications such as anemia and bone-mineral changes, especially in G3b.</li>
				<li><strong>G4:</strong> Severely reduced function. Planning for kidney replacement therapy (dialysis or transplant) is usually discussed with a nephrologist.</li>
				<li><strong>G5:</strong> Kidney failure. Many people at this level need dialysis or a transplant, although some choose conservative management.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Which eGFR equation is used for staging?</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Staging uses an eGFR equation, not Cockcroft-Gault. The 2021 CKD-EPI creatinine equation
				is the current standard in the United States, as described on our
				<a href="/methodology" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">methodology page</a>.
				Cockcroft-Gault reports creatinine clearance in mL/min and is not indexed to body surface
				area, so its values should not be placed directly on the G1&ndash;G5 scale. See
				<a href="/egfr-vs-creatinine-clearance" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">eGFR vs creatinine clearance</a>
				for the difference.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Sources</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				<li>KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease. <em>Kidney International</em>. 2024;105(4S):S117&ndash;S314.</li>
				<li>Inker LA, et al. New Creatinine- and Cystatin C&ndash;Based Equations to Estimate GFR without Race. <em>N Engl J Med</em>. 2021;385:1737&ndash;1749.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="mt-12"><MedicalDisclaimer /></div>
			<RelatedLinks exclude="/ckd-stages" />
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
